1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:39,877 --> 00:01:41,287
Um...

17
00:01:41,287 --> 00:01:44,877
This is our final co-conspirator.

18
00:01:44,877 --> 00:01:47,667
I'm Martin Liebert of Lemerio Trading.

19
00:01:48,877 --> 00:01:50,877
I'm N-Norah Arendt.

20
00:01:51,347 --> 00:01:53,437
Let's not waste any time.

21
00:01:53,927 --> 00:01:57,267
After all, business is like fresh fish in a kitchen.

22
00:01:58,887 --> 00:02:02,217
If we aren't quick about things, everything will go to waste.

23
00:02:15,697 --> 00:02:18,617
Will everything go according to plan?

24
00:02:28,217 --> 00:02:31,847
If we fail, there won't be a future ahead of us.

25
00:02:39,227 --> 00:02:44,227
Wolf and a Pack of Pups

26
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:49,397
You must be kidding.

27
00:02:49,817 --> 00:02:51,767
The sun hasn't even set.

28
00:02:52,157 --> 00:02:53,817
Well, that's because...

29
00:02:53,817 --> 00:02:57,467
I'm going ahead of you. Catch up as soon as you can.

30
00:02:58,997 --> 00:03:00,537
S-Sir!

31
00:03:00,537 --> 00:03:05,227
It's okay. He's just ignorant about shepherds and how dangerous the roads can be at night.

32
00:03:06,627 --> 00:03:09,707
He's shouldering the very future of Lemerio Trading.

33
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:11,457
It's to be expected.

34
00:03:25,897 --> 00:03:28,067
The stars are really pretty.

35
00:03:28,707 --> 00:03:30,237
They look all right.

36
00:03:30,237 --> 00:03:33,207
They're far prettier in my homeland.

37
00:03:34,447 --> 00:03:39,117
Who'd have thought we'd be able to talk about something so trivial under these circumstances?

38
00:03:41,077 --> 00:03:44,167
You won't last long if you're always uptight.

39
00:03:44,167 --> 00:03:45,957
Yeah, you're right.

40
00:03:48,457 --> 00:03:51,287
Tomorrow we'll arrive at that forbidden passage.

41
00:04:06,767 --> 00:04:09,707
It feels like just about anything could show up here.

42
00:04:10,357 --> 00:04:12,607
If we encounter wolves, do not panic.

43
00:04:12,947 --> 00:04:15,727
I guarantee that I'll deliver you safely to town.

44
00:04:21,247 --> 00:04:23,617
May God be with us.

45
00:04:36,217 --> 00:04:37,047
Hey.

46
00:04:37,967 --> 00:04:40,427
Do you think we'll be safe from the wolves?

47
00:04:40,427 --> 00:04:41,887
Not a chance.

48
00:04:41,887 --> 00:04:43,337
We're already surrounded.

49
00:04:43,677 --> 00:04:44,927
What?

50
00:04:46,517 --> 00:04:50,967
Well, even if that were to happen, I could guarantee your safety.

51
00:04:51,477 --> 00:04:53,787
I can't say the same about the others.

52
00:04:56,657 --> 00:04:59,117
We'll be in trouble unless everyone's okay.

53
00:04:59,617 --> 00:05:01,697
I truly don't know if that's possible.

54
00:05:02,327 --> 00:05:04,787
The forest is in the direction of the wind.

55
00:05:04,787 --> 00:05:09,697
If wolves are out there, they're sharpening their fangs in anticipation of a sheep feast.

56
00:05:24,477 --> 00:05:25,927
That's a smart dog.

57
00:05:26,767 --> 00:05:28,767
It's really getting on my nerves.

58
00:05:28,767 --> 00:05:30,017
What do you mean by that?

59
00:05:31,107 --> 00:05:34,487
That dog knows who I really am and is trying to intimidate me.

60
00:05:34,897 --> 00:05:36,147
Is that so?

61
00:05:36,147 --> 00:05:39,817
Good grief. He really doesn't know his place.

62
00:05:42,907 --> 00:05:45,027
Do you think Norah has noticed?

63
00:05:46,827 --> 00:05:51,327
If the smuggling fails, Norah will be worse off than all of us.

64
00:05:51,837 --> 00:05:55,367
If we keep quiet, there's a possibility that we can escape, but...

65
00:05:55,837 --> 00:05:59,457
Geez, you really are obsessed with blondes, aren't you?

66
00:05:59,457 --> 00:06:02,257
I told you what kind of punishment she could get, didn't I?

67
00:06:03,057 --> 00:06:06,267
There's no way a frail girl like her could bear something like that.

68
00:06:06,947 --> 00:06:11,597
In that case, you should protect her with all your might.

69
00:06:14,727 --> 00:06:15,597
Holo...

70
00:06:34,917 --> 00:06:36,917
I hope the wolves won't show up while we're here.

71
00:06:36,917 --> 00:06:40,087
Oh, yes, indeed.

72
00:06:40,087 --> 00:06:43,917
We should arrive at Lamtra by noon if we leave at daybreak.

73
00:06:43,917 --> 00:06:47,207
The rest will be up to me from there on out.

74
00:06:47,207 --> 00:06:49,627
I'm going to prepare for tomorrow by getting some sleep.

75
00:06:52,227 --> 00:06:53,637
Sleep well.

76
00:07:34,937 --> 00:07:36,427
Lawrence-san, stay back.

77
00:07:42,907 --> 00:07:44,817
There's no need to panic.

78
00:07:48,537 --> 00:07:50,837
Wake up and stay alert.

79
00:08:27,447 --> 00:08:28,707
Did you manage to drive them away?

80
00:08:29,237 --> 00:08:31,737
They're no longer nearby.

81
00:08:33,207 --> 00:08:36,077
The wolves around here are always like this.

82
00:08:36,077 --> 00:08:39,197
They don't ever howl or show signs they're about to attack.

83
00:08:40,207 --> 00:08:43,917
It just always feels like they're watching us.

84
00:08:46,217 --> 00:08:49,417
True. It's strange that they don't howl.

85
00:09:01,947 --> 00:09:03,817
I hope things turn out well.

86
00:09:05,527 --> 00:09:06,707
As do I.

87
00:09:10,827 --> 00:09:15,577
Um... Do you know a lot about wolves, Miss Holo?

88
00:09:18,577 --> 00:09:25,787
Oh, it's just that you seemed to notice the wolves rather quickly last night.

89
00:09:26,117 --> 00:09:29,427
You think? I somehow realized they were there, that's all.

90
00:09:29,427 --> 00:09:30,847
Really?

91
00:09:31,217 --> 00:09:36,757
Maybe I was simply feeling tense.
The men with us are useless, after all.

92
00:09:37,637 --> 00:09:38,877
Don't you think so, too?

93
00:09:40,227 --> 00:09:42,357
N-Not at all.

94
00:09:43,437 --> 00:09:45,977
What do you think about this one?

95
00:09:49,737 --> 00:09:51,447
Don't mind him.

96
00:09:51,447 --> 00:09:53,227
Say whatever comes to mind.

97
00:09:59,957 --> 00:10:03,197
You've figured him out pretty well.

98
00:10:05,587 --> 00:10:08,857
Well, it's ridiculous to ask a woman who's traveling with a man

99
00:10:08,857 --> 00:10:12,467
whether she knows a thing or two about wolves.

100
00:10:12,467 --> 00:10:13,927
Why's that?

101
00:10:14,247 --> 00:10:20,397
Come nighttime, a male wolf will always appearâ€”
tempted by this helpless, adorable rabbit.

102
00:10:22,057 --> 00:10:27,437
Surely you'll agree that a rabbit who is devoured by a wolf every night couldn't fail to know something about them!

103
00:10:28,027 --> 00:10:31,447
Um... Does that mean...

104
00:10:32,647 --> 00:10:33,857
What a cute reaction.

105
00:10:34,407 --> 00:10:36,947
In our case, it's the opposite.

106
00:10:36,947 --> 00:10:41,487
My companion is the true rabbit. If I left him on his own, he'd likely die of loneliness.

107
00:10:42,537 --> 00:10:48,047
In any case, the fact that I quickly noticed the wolves was just a coincidence.

108
00:10:48,047 --> 00:10:51,597
I thought you may have been a shepherd, Holo-san.

109
00:10:52,467 --> 00:10:54,407
That's surprising to hear.

110
00:10:55,507 --> 00:10:59,557
It's because Enek seemed very interested in you.

111
00:10:59,557 --> 00:11:03,057
Oh, I bet he's fallen in love with me.

112
00:11:03,897 --> 00:11:06,137
Enek has?

113
00:11:06,527 --> 00:11:09,597
You think dearly of him, don't you?

114
00:11:10,107 --> 00:11:15,527
He thinks he's secured your affection because of all the attention you give him.

115
00:11:15,527 --> 00:11:20,407
I'm sure he's falling into selfishness and seeking the attention of others.

116
00:11:20,787 --> 00:11:22,957
You should act indifferent once in a while.

117
00:11:22,957 --> 00:11:24,657
That's how you handle his reins.

118
00:11:25,587 --> 00:11:30,417
I'll be sure to follow your advice if he flirts with another.

119
00:11:30,417 --> 00:11:31,417
That's good.

120
00:11:33,007 --> 00:11:37,877
I want to indulge him as much as I can right now, though.

121
00:11:39,097 --> 00:11:46,467
This will be my last job as a shepherd regardless of whether or not we're successful.

122
00:11:48,727 --> 00:11:51,777
Do you still have concerns about her?

123
00:11:51,777 --> 00:11:52,807
You win.

124
00:12:25,307 --> 00:12:26,717
You sure got it done.

125
00:12:27,107 --> 00:12:30,277
I'm so glad! I thought you might have come back empty-handed.

126
00:12:30,277 --> 00:12:32,057
Is that how I looked?

127
00:12:32,437 --> 00:12:35,397
Anyone holding such a large sum of money would look tense.

128
00:12:35,947 --> 00:12:37,407
Sorry for losing my composure.

129
00:12:37,407 --> 00:12:38,907
Let's be on our way.

130
00:12:41,827 --> 00:12:45,477
A golden tomorrow awaits the four of us.

131
00:12:53,717 --> 00:12:56,557
I-Is this really the same path we traveled on?

132
00:12:57,797 --> 00:13:00,247
I-It seems really different.

133
00:13:00,967 --> 00:13:02,087
Enek!

134
00:13:02,097 --> 00:13:04,597
Sorry, but we need to hurry.

135
00:13:09,757 --> 00:13:11,187
Have they arrived?

136
00:13:11,187 --> 00:13:13,647
Yes, they're on top of the hill over there.

137
00:13:17,817 --> 00:13:20,327
W-Will we be all right?

138
00:13:20,327 --> 00:13:22,987
Yes, but we need to hurry!

139
00:13:25,407 --> 00:13:26,367
Enek!

140
00:13:28,777 --> 00:13:31,037
This girl knows what she's doing.

141
00:13:31,037 --> 00:13:34,397
The wolves can't do anything now.

142
00:13:34,397 --> 00:13:35,577
What do you mean?

143
00:13:35,577 --> 00:13:40,337
Wolves won't move in a way that will allow one of their own to get injured.

144
00:13:40,337 --> 00:13:45,467
They'll carefully surround their prey and wait for the best opportunity to attack.

145
00:13:45,927 --> 00:13:47,007
Enek!

146
00:13:49,267 --> 00:13:53,637
This formation will allow us to slay one at the very least.

147
00:13:54,447 --> 00:13:59,147
We'll be able to make it at this pace because wolves will never attack alone.

148
00:14:02,327 --> 00:14:03,537
In the trees.

149
00:14:03,537 --> 00:14:04,357
What is it?

150
00:14:15,507 --> 00:14:17,257
It's now or never!

151
00:14:23,967 --> 00:14:24,717
Stay back!

152
00:14:38,937 --> 00:14:43,017
I hear that humans sometimes grumble about the reckless youths of this generation.

153
00:14:44,607 --> 00:14:47,147
I feel the same way about these wolves.

154
00:14:49,747 --> 00:14:50,997
Are we safe now?

155
00:14:50,997 --> 00:14:53,117
N-Norah-san, answer me.

156
00:14:53,537 --> 00:14:56,377
I don't know, but I'll do my best.

157
00:14:56,377 --> 00:14:57,787
Give me a break!

158
00:15:42,297 --> 00:15:43,177
Listen.

159
00:15:44,637 --> 00:15:47,207
I'm the only one who can handle this.

160
00:15:47,597 --> 00:15:51,967
Stay clear of me after you tell the girl and the young man to go ahead of us.

161
00:15:53,437 --> 00:15:54,807
Why change course now?

162
00:15:56,937 --> 00:16:00,147
Didn't I say they weren't normal wolves?

163
00:16:01,317 --> 00:16:04,647
The pack won't chase the sheep if you do as I say.

164
00:16:05,117 --> 00:16:07,367
They weren't after the sheep in the first place.

165
00:16:09,157 --> 00:16:11,037
Cheap bluster.

166
00:16:11,037 --> 00:16:13,027
Crude pride.

167
00:16:14,037 --> 00:16:18,047
Ideals that the young have always valued.

168
00:16:21,417 --> 00:16:24,337
Come on. They won't move unless you tell them to.

169
00:16:24,797 --> 00:16:27,247
Partners should cooperate, should they not?

170
00:16:31,587 --> 00:16:33,797
We'll hold them here.

171
00:16:33,807 --> 00:16:37,037
You two go ahead with the gold as planned.

172
00:16:38,067 --> 00:16:38,897
But...

173
00:16:38,897 --> 00:16:40,847
No, we should leave it to them.

174
00:16:41,237 --> 00:16:43,737
Let's meet at the walls of Lubinheigen.

175
00:16:43,737 --> 00:16:45,727
We'll all be rich by then.

176
00:16:49,697 --> 00:16:50,907
Good luck.

177
00:17:01,927 --> 00:17:04,117
Stay a fair distance away from me.

178
00:17:04,467 --> 00:17:06,767
It might go badly if you get too close.

179
00:17:07,927 --> 00:17:09,157
You understand, don't you?

180
00:17:12,427 --> 00:17:14,637
Don't you dare lose.

181
00:17:19,267 --> 00:17:23,327
Were you a proper male, I'd at least get a kiss for my trouble here.

182
00:17:24,187 --> 00:17:25,147
Oh, that's right.

183
00:17:25,147 --> 00:17:26,887
Hold on to this for me.

184
00:17:31,537 --> 00:17:35,997
I'd like to resolve things peacefully,
but I don't think I can make any promises.

185
00:17:36,867 --> 00:17:41,077
If I have no clothes when we go to meet the others,
I'll be cold and you'll be troubled, I should think.

186
00:17:47,177 --> 00:17:48,797
I'll see you soon.

187
00:17:57,957 --> 00:18:00,427
You must keep going, Norah-san.

188
00:18:00,957 --> 00:18:02,887
Do you want their deaths to be in vain?

189
00:18:03,647 --> 00:18:05,027
Deaths?

190
00:18:05,027 --> 00:18:05,977
Excuse me.

191
00:18:06,487 --> 00:18:09,557
Let's hurry so we can repay their bravery.

192
00:18:42,477 --> 00:18:45,937
Is that all you had to say?

193
00:18:50,027 --> 00:18:52,567
I knew all of you were just a bunch of pups

194
00:18:52,567 --> 00:18:54,937
baring your teeth for no good reason.

195
00:19:14,927 --> 00:19:15,757
Holo!

196
00:19:27,217 --> 00:19:28,737
Lawrence-san?

197
00:19:28,737 --> 00:19:29,987
Um, yes.

198
00:19:30,567 --> 00:19:32,357
You were safe after all.

199
00:19:32,357 --> 00:19:34,327
Liebert told us everything.

200
00:19:34,327 --> 00:19:39,607
We'd been waiting at the edge of the forest just in case, and we
decided we should look for you when we heard what happened.

201
00:19:40,247 --> 00:19:41,497
I see.

202
00:19:42,117 --> 00:19:46,117
I was drying my clothes in the brush since they were wet from the deluge.

203
00:19:48,167 --> 00:19:50,917
Lawrence-san, where's your partner?

204
00:19:51,837 --> 00:19:53,127
She isn't here.

205
00:19:54,387 --> 00:19:55,797
That's reassuring to hear.

206
00:20:02,767 --> 00:20:05,887
I won't ask you not to take this personally.

207
00:20:07,357 --> 00:20:08,817
You're betraying us?

208
00:20:08,817 --> 00:20:10,887
Lemerio Trading is betraying us?

209
00:20:10,897 --> 00:20:12,057
It's just insurance.

210
00:20:12,657 --> 00:20:16,367
It weighed heavy on us to hear that there would be a woman with you.

211
00:20:16,367 --> 00:20:18,277
We're relieved to see that's not the case.

212
00:20:18,277 --> 00:20:22,117
This might sound like an excuse, but we're in the same position you are.

213
00:20:22,117 --> 00:20:25,497
We have to eliminate any danger we can.

214
00:20:25,497 --> 00:20:27,197
You thought I'd blackmail you?

215
00:20:27,707 --> 00:20:31,087
Such a huge amount of money could cloud anyone's eyes.

216
00:20:31,087 --> 00:20:33,497
Those who choose the path of business know this.

217
00:20:34,047 --> 00:20:36,997
I'll give you back your companion's memento.

218
00:20:39,767 --> 00:20:44,647
I regret that I'm not able to say we'll meet again,

219
00:20:46,887 --> 00:20:50,517
and it's depressing to think what's going to happen later.

220
00:20:50,527 --> 00:20:51,607
Hey!

221
00:20:51,607 --> 00:20:53,277
Don't you feel the same way?

222
00:20:53,277 --> 00:20:56,237
Isn't she the girl he picked to do the job?

223
00:20:56,237 --> 00:20:57,367
You can't mean...

224
00:21:00,077 --> 00:21:00,817
Look what you did.

225
00:21:01,247 --> 00:21:02,567
You shouldn't have moved.

226
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:14,967
Why don't we tie the girl up like this poor bastard?

227
00:21:14,967 --> 00:21:16,627
The wolves will finish them off.

228
00:21:16,627 --> 00:21:20,557
You fool! She uses pagan witchcraft, you know.

229
00:21:20,557 --> 00:21:23,727
She'll manage to survive even if you blindfold her and tie her hands.

230
00:21:23,727 --> 00:21:26,047
And if that happens, it'll be the end of us.

231
00:21:26,057 --> 00:21:29,187
It doesn't feel right to have to kill a girl like that.

232
00:21:29,187 --> 00:21:30,177
Stop bringing it up!

233
00:21:30,857 --> 00:21:31,687
Sorry.

234
00:21:34,027 --> 00:21:35,687
Should we finish him off?

235
00:21:35,697 --> 00:21:37,317
What, you wanna do it?

236
00:21:37,317 --> 00:21:40,447
No, the less blood on our hands, the better.

237
00:21:40,777 --> 00:21:42,077
I agree.

238
00:21:42,077 --> 00:21:45,867
Let's go. Liebert-san will be upset if we don't hurry.

239
00:21:45,867 --> 00:21:49,027
His female partner is probably dead by now.

240
00:23:40,677 --> 00:23:44,937
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a New Journey."</i>

241
00:23:45,557 --> 00:23:50,017
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a New Journey."</i>

